WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:11.400
append reads cached keys and values for each lane, then writes the next token slot. cached is the number of old tokens, width the values per token, and capacity the allocated token slots.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.360
The printed byte count accounts for requested payload, not measured memory traffic.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.190
Read history.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.370
Accumulate old keys and values.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.680
Append token.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.585
Write the new key and value slot.

00:00:24.585 --> 00:00:25.510
Read back.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:28.935
Inspect the accumulated result on the CPU.

00:00:30.435 --> 00:00:34.940
The key-value cache here is an application data structure in device memory.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.845
It is distinct from the GPU’s L1 and L2 hardware caches.

00:00:38.845 --> 00:00:42.280
Longer histories request more old key and value data.
